cards.text:
Derivatives: NH₂OH → {{c1::oxime}}
NH₂NH₂ → {{c2::hydrazone}}
C₆H₅NHNH₂ → {{c3::phenylhydrazone}}
NH₂NHCONH₂ → {{c4::semicarbazone}}
RNH₂ → {{c5::Schiff’s base (substituted imine)}}.

Origins: formic acid from {{c1::red ants (formica)}}
acetic acid from {{c2::vinegar (acetum)}}
butyric acid from {{c3::rancid butter (butyrum)}}.

Common → IUPAC: oxalic = {{c1::ethanedioic}}
malonic = {{c2::propanedioic}}
succinic = {{c3::butanedioic}}
glutaric = {{c4::pentanedioic}}
adipic = {{c5::hexanedioic}}.

Uses: methanoic acid in {{c1::rubber, textile, leather, electroplating}}
hexanedioic acid for {{c2::nylon-6,6}}
sodium benzoate as a {{c3::food preservative}}
higher fatty acids for {{c4::soaps and detergents}}.

